      <span style="background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.12); color: #c084fc; border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">STATUTORY CLEARANCE</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory Interstate e-Way Bills, Regulatory Clearances &amp; 100% Marine Insurance for sofa transport from bangalore to tumkur</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When you ship a sofa from Bangalore to Tumkur, the journey is governed by a set of statutory transit documents that safeguard both the cargo and the consignor.</p>

<p>First, the <strong>GST e‑Way bill</strong> is mandatory for all goods crossing state borders. This electronic waybill, generated through the GST portal, records the value, description, and destination of the sofa, ensuring tax compliance and enabling real‑time tracking for the carrier.</p>

<p>Second, the carrier must provide an <strong>IBA‑approved Lorry Receipt (LR/Bilty)</strong>. This document, signed by the driver and the consignor, confirms the hand‑over of the sofa, its condition at loading, and the agreed freight rate. It serves as a receipt and a legal proof of transport, useful in case of disputes or damage claims.</p>

<p>Finally, to protect against unforeseen events, a <strong>100 % declared‑value IRDAI marine transit insurance</strong> is recommended. Though the sofa travels on land, this marine policy covers accidental collision, theft, or delays caused by weather, strikes, or other disruptions. The insurer pays the full declared value, ensuring you are compensated for any loss or damage.</p>

